WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.130
- One of the hallmarks of
the American legal system

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:05.350
is that anyone can file
a lawsuit for any reason

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:06.487
at any time.

00:00:06.487 --> 00:00:08.728
("The Star Spangled Banner" playing)

00:00:08.728 --> 00:00:10.530
(fireworks)

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.680
and, of course, one of the major drawbacks

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:14.600
to the American legal system is

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.533
anyone can file any lawsuit
at any time for any reason.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:21.270
Doesn't mean they're going to win,

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.150
but they can still file the lawsuit.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.400
And over the years, many people have

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.020
taken advantage of this principle to file

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.960
a whole variety of frivolous lawsuits.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.650
Now, many of these cases are filed

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.290
by self-represented parties,

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:33.090
but you'll also find far too many lawyers

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.110
willing to attach their
names and reputations

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:36.612
to these suits.

00:00:36.612 --> 00:00:40.020
(mock sneezing)

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:40.853
Sorry.

00:00:40.853 --> 00:00:42.130
Must be getting over something.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.240
But baseless lawsuits not
only waste the precious time

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.250
of an already overloaded court system,

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.930
they can also be financially ruinous

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:51.070
to the parties having to defend
these nonsensical claims.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.360
But these cases also have
the unfortunate side effect

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:56.110
of making us lawyer
types look kind of bad.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:59.030
But today let's take a
mirror to our own profession

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:00.976
and let's discuss five
of the dumbest lawsuits

00:01:00.976 --> 00:01:02.371
ever filed.

00:01:02.371 --> 00:01:05.070
(upbeat music)

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.990
Sponsored by Skillshare.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:08.270
So where do we begin?

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.270
Well, when someone tries to sue another

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:11.700
for a substantial sum of money,

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.372
we refer to that as suing
the pants off of someone.

00:01:14.372 --> 00:01:15.205
(grunts)

00:01:15.205 --> 00:01:16.038
(popping)

00:01:16.038 --> 00:01:18.270
But that can literally be the case.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:21.010
And in 2005, Roy L. Pearson Jr.,

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:24.340
a lawyer and newly appointed
DC administrative law judge

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:25.810
took that phrase quite literally

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:29.400
after Custom Cleaners, a DC
dry cleaning establishment,

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.340
briefly misplaced his pants.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:32.730
The store prominently displayed a sign

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.490
that said satisfaction guaranteed,

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:36.920
and Judge Pearson demanded satisfaction

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:40.230
by suing the owners for $67 million.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.990
So here's the backstory of what
has become the poster child

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.750
for frivolous pants-related litigation.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.070
In 2005, Judge Pearson took
a pair of expensive pants

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:50.370
to Custom Cleaners.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.900
The business was owned
by Jin and Soo Chung,

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:55.850
Korean immigrants who came
to the United States in 1992.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.030
Now Judge Pearson intended
to wear these pants

00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:59.900
on his first week on the bench.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.510
But the business owners had inadvertently

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:03.440
sent the pants to the wrong location.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:04.940
But Judge Pearson refused to accept them,

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:06.450
claiming that they were not his pants,

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.370
despite the owners providing confirmation

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:10.230
through their business records, tags

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.490
and the judge's receipt.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:15.470
Now Pearson demanded payment of $1,150.

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:17.180
The owners did not respond to this demand,

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:19.120
so Judge Pearson then filed suit,

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.290
no pun intended,

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:22.667
in the District of
Columbia Superior Court for

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:25.380
$67.3 million in damages,

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:30.130
67,000 times more than his
original settlement demand.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:32.020
Judge Pearson contended that the Chungs

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.650
had failed to honor the legal warranty

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:35.420
established by the same day service

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:39.370
and satisfaction guaranteed
signs displayed at their store.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:41.940
Judge Pearson apparently had
an incredibly expensive view

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.640
of the idea of satisfaction guaranteed,

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.350
which he claimed obligated the Chungs

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:49.010
to undertake any and all
actions without limitation

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.360
based on the customer's determination

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.720
of whatever would make
the customer satisfied.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.980
Given this expensive
and incredibly literal

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.110
interpretation of satisfaction guaranteed,

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.650
it sort of raises the question,

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.380
who was Judge Pearson's legal mentor?

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.400
Lionel Hutz?

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.246
- Mr. Hutz, do you know
you're not wearing any pants?

00:03:05.246 --> 00:03:06.115
- What?

00:03:06.115 --> 00:03:07.390
(screams)

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:08.670
- Well, Judge Pearson contended

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:11.250
that the Chung's failure to
provide him proper satisfaction

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:12.970
constituted seven separate violations

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:15.380
of Washington DC consumer protection laws,

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.170
and using a complicated formula,

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.810
Judge Pearson argued that
the owners and their son,

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:24.010
Ki Chung, owed each $18,000 per day

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:25.810
that the judge was not satisfied,

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.960
and they had failed to provide
him with same day service.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:32.080
As part of his damages,
Pearson also claimed $90,000

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.550
to rent a car to drive
to another dry cleaner

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:36.910
and $3 million in emotional distress,

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:39.140
because you know, he
really loved those pants.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:41.490
But Judge Pearson is
not an unreasonable man.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.660
Before trial, Judge
Pearson generously lowered

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.240
this damage claims to $54 million.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.540
When this case went to trial,

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:51.050
it actually went to trial in 2007,

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:52.590
the DC Superior Court rejected

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:54.230
all of Judge Pearson's claims.

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.470
The court ruled that Judge Pearson

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.250
had failed to prove that Custom Cleaners

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:00.720
had misled consumers with a
satisfaction guaranteed sign.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.700
In fact, the court
found that Judge Pearson

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.780
was unable to prove that the cleaners

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.670
lost his pants in the first place,

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.560
and further, the court
held that Judge Pearson's

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.270
expansive interpretation
of satisfaction guaranteed

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.240
had no support under the law.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:14.073
Shocker.

00:04:14.073 --> 00:04:16.200
Pearson appealed, but
lost on appeal as well.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.750
And because this is America,
although the Chungs prevailed,

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.910
they were financially
devastated by the litigation,

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:23.040
and they were only able to
afford their attorney's fees

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:25.220
after a generous outpouring
of financial support

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:26.670
through third-party fundraising.

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:29.100
In September, 2007,
citing a loss of revenue

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:29.933
and emotional distress,

00:04:29.933 --> 00:04:32.670
the Chungs closed and sold
their dry cleaning shop

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.150
at the center of the dispute.

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:36.140
And they decided to focus their energy on

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:37.980
another dry cleaning shop that they owned.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.700
And as for Judge Pearson,

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:42.650
well, he did not get
to be judge much longer

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:45.770
as he was not reappointed when
his two year term expired.

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:47.780
Over a decade later, former Judge Pearson

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:48.613
was brought before

00:04:48.613 --> 00:04:50.100
the DC Board of
Professional Responsibility

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:53.330
to address his bizarre
behavior in the pants lawsuit.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:55.850
And on June 4th, 2020, the
Board suspended Pearson

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:58.010
from practicing law for 90 days.

00:04:58.010 --> 00:04:59.880
The Board characterized
Pearson's damage theories

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.870
as utterly frivolous and excoriated him

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:04.490
for his refusal to accept
reasonable settlement offers.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.300
The Board concluded that
Pearson had violated

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.387
the ethical rule prohibiting
conduct, which quote,

00:05:08.387 --> 00:05:11.680
"Seriously interferes with the
administration of justice."

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.730
Which takes us to our next
incredibly frivolous lawsuit.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:16.720
Because in today's image-obsessed culture,

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:19.000
people will try anything
to fight the aging process.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.970
Trendy diets, experimental remedies,

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:23.790
whatever it is that keeps Paul
Rudd from getting any older.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.500
But in 2018, a 69-year old Dutchman

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.610
was perhaps the first
person to turn the fight

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:31.250
against the aging process into a legal one

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:35.130
by asking a judge to legally
reduce his age by 20 years.

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:36.930
This did not go well.

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:39.390
But meet Emile Ratelband,
a motivational speaker

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:42.120
and self-described positivity
trainer from the Netherlands.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.880
In 2018, the then 69-year old Ratelband

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.130
appeared before a Dutch court

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.660
complaining that he had been the victim

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:49.430
of age discrimination in employment,

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:52.120
and through unfair denial of Tinder dates.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.990
But instead of filing suit
against specific people

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:56.570
or entities that might have wronged him,

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:59.240
Ratelband took novel approach
to remedy his alleged injury

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:02.250
by asking a Dutch court to
legally change his birthday

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:06.320
from March 11th, 1949 to March 11th, 1969

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.430
in order to make him 20 years younger.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.200
Describing himself as a quote "young god,"

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.060
Ratelband argued that his
strict diet, exercise routine,

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.430
and mental discipline had,
according to his doctors,

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:18.760
given him the body of a 45-year-old.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:20.440
- The judge was first laughing,

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.730
and then I told him the series matter,

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.620
and then he said, "Well, you have a point.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:26.420
Perhaps I want to be younger also."

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:28.830
- In a move that was sure
not to offend anyone,

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:30.160
Ratelband likened his struggles

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.567
to that of transgender
people saying quote,

00:06:32.567 --> 00:06:34.450
"We live in a time when
you can change your name

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:35.300
and change your gender.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.570
Why can't I decide my own age?"

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:39.250
And in a generous offer,

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.750
Ratelband even stated that he was ready

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:43.820
to give up his 1500 Euro per month pension

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.140
in return for the Dutch government

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:47.490
shaving 20 years off of his official age.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:48.820
Not surprisingly, the court ultimately

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:49.900
ruled against Ratelband,

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:51.530
holding that there was no legal mechanism

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:54.070
for allowing a person to
change their date of birth.

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:55.370
And in its ruling, the court warned

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:57.371
that allowing Ratelband to
change his date of birth

00:06:57.371 --> 00:06:59.260
would create all kinds of legal problems

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:01.510
by effectively erasing 20 years of events.

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:04.550
Quote, "Mr. Ratelband is at
Liberty to feel 20 years younger

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:06.350
than his real age and to act accordingly,

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:08.300
but amending his date of birth would cause

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:10.640
20 years of records to vanish
from the register of births,

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:13.870
deaths and marriages and
registered partnerships.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:16.030
This would have a variety
of undesirable legal

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.440
and societal implications.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:20.270
The priority must be to ensure
that the public registers

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:22.600
contain accurate factual information."

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:24.160
The court highlighted that specific dates

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:26.820
and obligations attached to
age, such as the right to vote

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:29.380
right to marry, drink
alcohol and drive a car,

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:31.220
and that a ruling in favor of Ratelband

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:32.280
could open up the possibility

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:34.520
of a person declaring oneself older

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.410
and try to obtain those rights.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:38.730
Which pisses me off just because
I didn't think about that,

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:40.440
and I really would've
liked to have done that.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:41.790
But if Ratelband feels like

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:43.450
he has been discriminated against,

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:45.360
the ruling said that there were other laws

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:46.510
that he could use to invoke

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:48.490
and try to seek relief that way.

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:51.510
Because at the end of the day,
he only has himself to blame,

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:54.810
which is also the case in
our next frivolous lawsuit.

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:56.750
Our next plaintiff took
it one step further

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.410
and just sued himself.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.260
Because many people who
represent themself pro se

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:03.980
are filed by those currently
serving time in prison.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:05.990
And many of those lawsuits try to address

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:07.310
a variety of important issues,

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:08.850
like subpar prison conditions,

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:11.770
or particularly in case
of death row inmates,

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:14.120
to seek a retrial of one's case.

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:16.910
Other times, they're just plain weird.

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:19.290
And such was the case of Robert Lee Brock,

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:21.960
the man who sued himself for $5 million

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.050
for violating his own civil rights.

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:24.890
Here's the story.

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:28.580
In 1995 Brock was serving
a 23 year prison sentence

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:30.190
at the Indian Creek Correctional Center

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.600
in Chesapeake, Virginia
for breaking and entering

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:33.780
and grand larceny.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.470
And like many people
who make bad decisions

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:38.290
that they regret forever,
he was drunk at the time.

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:42.685
- To alcohol, the cause of and solution to

00:08:42.685 --> 00:08:44.800
all of life's problems.

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:46.100
- And for that, Brock believed

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:48.290
You may be entitled to compensation.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:49.260
Who me?

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:50.093
Yes, you.

00:08:50.093 --> 00:08:51.400
You could get compensation.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:53.110
Wow, that sounds great,
I think I'll do that.

00:08:53.110 --> 00:08:55.470
Because in a seven page
handwritten complaint,

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:57.130
Brock argued that his Christian faith

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:58.780
forbids him from drinking alcohol,

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:01.332
and he argued that getting drunk
caused him to commit crimes

00:09:01.332 --> 00:09:04.310
and violate his own
religious civil rights.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:07.570
He pleaded with the court to
grant him relief from himself,

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:09.380
quote "For violating my religious beliefs,

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.550
I want to pay myself $5 million,

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.520
but ask the state to pay it on my behalf

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:16.980
since I can't work and
am a ward of the state."

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:19.150
Brock sought $3 million
for his wife and children,

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:21.720
quote "for their pain and
suffering and college tuition,"

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:23.490
and $2 million to support him

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:25.190
for the next 23 years in prison,

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:27.550
but promised he would pay it back someday.

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:30.300
The judge was not impressed

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.910
and immediately dismissed
the lawsuit as frivolous.

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:34.277
In her order, the judge wrote quote,

00:09:34.277 --> 00:09:36.470
"Plaintiff has presented
an innovative approach

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:37.760
to civil rights litigation.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:40.030
However, his claim and
especially the relief sought

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:41.340
are totally ludicrous."

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:43.750
But Brock, who would later
file lawsuits under the alias

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:46.040
Two Souls Walker, would continue to be

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:47.960
a thorn in the side of
the federal court system,

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:51.690
filing 29 appeals to Fourth
Circuit Court of Appeals

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:54.630
in 1995 through 1996 alone,

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:56.650
all of which were rejected.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.860
But Brock's barrage of baseless lawsuits

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.070
included complaints about
the price of coffee,

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:03.590
improper placement of a
mirror for the handicapped,

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:07.260
and suing the prison for $1
million for mental cruelty

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:09.520
when prison nurses said
no to Brock's request

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:10.750
for extra meat with dinner,

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.120
and vitamins in place of vegetables.

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:14.960
Brock even sued the victim of the crime

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.610
that originally sent him to jail.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:18.060
But in his final lawsuit,

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:19.367
Brock alleged that he was quote,

00:10:19.367 --> 00:10:21.760
"Either being poisoned or experimented on"

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.300
by the prison, because the
pancake syrup he was being served

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:27.850
contained propylene
glycol, a food additive

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:30.210
that does also happen to be contained

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:33.080
in some items like
deodorant and antifreeze.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:36.130
But it was the syrup that
broke the camel's back

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:37.340
as the Fourth Circuit Court of Appeals

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:39.460
decided that it had finally had enough.

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:41.120
The court ruled the case was frivolous,

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:42.990
not only because of the propylene glycol

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.180
is a common nontoxic extract,

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:47.010
but also Brock made no allegation

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:50.200
the prison forced him to eat
the allegedly poisonous syrup.

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:52.070
Citing Brock's history of wasting money

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:53.580
and precious court resources,

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:55.890
the court banned him from
filing any more lawsuits

00:10:55.890 --> 00:10:57.800
without a judge first certifying

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:00.230
that his claim was not frivolous.

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:02.890
Because the Constitution
guarantees life and liberty,

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:05.440
but it doesn't guarantee a good time.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:08.060
And that's what takes as to
our next frivolous lawsuit.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:08.900
There's an old saying that

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:11.130
you can't believe
everything you see on TV,

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:12.770
and that's actually a
good rule to live by,

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:15.500
and it's especially true
when it comes to advertising,

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:18.280
because beer commercials
often present a fantasy

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:19.670
of beach parties, beautiful women,

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:21.390
and occasionally skateboarding dogs,

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:23.680
but most people understand
this image to be just that,

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:24.720
a fantasy.

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:26.560
But that's most people.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:28.240
Because, for one Michigan man,

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:31.100
he believed that Budweiser's
advertisements in the late 80s

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:33.440
were misleading their audience
with an explicit promise

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:35.020
of partying and fun times.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:37.640
And when there's a
will, there's a lawsuit.

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:41.470
So in 1991, Richard Overton,
representing himself,

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:43.550
sued Anheuser-Busch for $10,000,

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:45.070
alleging their advertisements caused him

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:48.260
emotional distress, mental
injury and financial loss.

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:49.860
And in support of these allegations,

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:51.770
over Overton cited the
company's Bud Light ads,

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.887
which he claimed promised
beer's ability to make quote,

00:11:54.887 --> 00:11:56.360
"Fantasies come to life,

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.200
fantasies involving tropical settings,

00:11:58.200 --> 00:11:59.910
and beautiful men and women engaged

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:01.490
in unrestricted merriment."

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:02.880
- Bye, Spuds.

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:03.713
Call me.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.730
- Overton alleged Anheuser-Busch's ads

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:10.040
violated Michigan's laws
against deceptive advertising

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.300
by presenting this fantasy as reality

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:14.270
while downplaying the destructive effects

00:12:14.270 --> 00:12:15.660
of drinking alcohol.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:18.780
The Michigan Court of Appeals
dismissed Overton's claims.

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:20.700
The court held that Anheuser-Busch's ads

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:22.600
portraying unrestricted merriment,

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:25.120
were merely quote, "Grandiose suggestions

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:26.700
constituting puffing,"

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:28.330
which is actually a legal term,

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:31.530
and could not be the basis
of an actionable fraud claim.

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:33.610
The court further concluded
that Anheuser-Busch

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:36.080
could not be held liable
for allegedly downplaying

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:38.810
the dangers of alcohol by
portraying the consumption

00:12:38.810 --> 00:12:41.010
of alcoholic beverages
in a positive light.

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:42.300
And according to the Michigan court,

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:44.280
the dangers inherent
in alcohol consumption

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:45.750
are well-known to the public.

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:48.280
As a result, Anheuser-Busch
had no affirmative duty

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:50.430
to disclose in its advertisements

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:52.600
risks that are already well-known.

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:56.450
And decades later, Overton
still stands by his lawsuit.

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:59.220
In a 2007 interview with
the Kalamazoo Gazette,

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:01.240
he rejected the
characterization of his image

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:02.940
as a sex starved loser,

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:05.210
who drinks Bud Light hoping
to find pretty girls.

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:07.700
Overton himself doesn't
actually drink alcohol

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:10.550
and has three children and
a wife for three decades.

00:13:10.550 --> 00:13:12.700
And according to Overton,
the spark for his lawsuit

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:16.210
was seeing his young children
captivated by Spuds McKenzie,

00:13:16.210 --> 00:13:17.450
the Budweiser dog.

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:18.933
- Crack open one of those BLs.

00:13:18.933 --> 00:13:20.420
I don't have thumbs.

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:21.253
(clinging)

00:13:21.253 --> 00:13:22.570
- He said, quote, "I looked at them

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:23.760
and I thought this isn't right.

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:25.380
Here are my kids being drawn into

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:27.790
part of a culture of alcohol
because of this advertising.

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:29.880
That's when I figured
something needed to be done."

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:30.713
And fair enough.

00:13:30.713 --> 00:13:32.530
I think a lot of people
would probably agree

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:33.460
with that sentiment.

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:35.730
In a way, society has come to Overton

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:38.633
because those kinds of
ads regarding alcohol

00:13:38.633 --> 00:13:41.270
are no longer really seen on TV.

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:42.689
But the solution to this issue

00:13:42.689 --> 00:13:46.440
wasn't going to be found in a
deceptive advertising lawsuit.

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:48.930
But unfortunately, some
people have learned

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.900
that if you don't like something on TV,

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:53.150
even if you file a frivolous lawsuit,

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:55.370
you can still cause
pain to the other side.

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:57.870
Because you can accuse
former president Donald Trump

00:13:57.870 --> 00:13:58.940
of a lot of things,

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:01.160
and in fact, I have actually
outlined a lot of things

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:03.220
that you can credibly
accuse Donald Trump of

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:04.940
in a variety of videos.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:07.850
But there's one thing that
you cannot credibly accuse

00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:09.130
former President Trump of,

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:11.480
and that's having a sense of humor.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:14.340
Because in 2013, Donald Trump
showcased his lack of humor

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:16.900
by hiring high-priced
lawyers to sue Bill Maher

00:14:16.900 --> 00:14:19.170
for $5 million over a joke.

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:21.980
Back when Donald Trump was
just a failed game show host,

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:23.540
he made a name for himself by questioning

00:14:23.540 --> 00:14:26.240
the Constitutional legitimacy
of president Barack Obama,

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:28.530
the first African-American
elected to the presidency.

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:31.660
And back in 2011, Trump
demanded the Barack Obama

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:33.250
release his long form birth certificate

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:35.100
to prove that he was born
in the United States.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.400
After Obama released
his birth certificate,

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:38.890
Trump continued to fan the flames

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:40.370
of racist conspiracy theories,

00:14:40.370 --> 00:14:42.410
and in the run-up to the 2012 election,

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:43.737
Donald Trump said that he would donate

00:14:43.737 --> 00:14:46.210
$5 million to charity if Obama released

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:48.740
all passport records
and college transcripts.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:52.580
And enter Bill Maher, host of
the eponymous HBO talk show

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:54.500
and in mocking Trump's demands

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:57.190
that Obama prove has
eligibility to be president,

00:14:57.190 --> 00:14:58.620
the comedy host demanded

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:01.690
that Donald Trump provide
his own proof of parentage,

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:03.167
namely, that he was not quote,

00:15:03.167 --> 00:15:05.340
"The love child of a human woman

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:08.060
and an orangutan from the Brooklyn zoo."

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:09.990
And on January 7th, 2013,

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:12.480
Bill Maher appeared on the
Tonight Show with Jay Leno,

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:13.990
where he continued to demand

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:17.040
that Donald Trump prove he
was not sired by a great ape.

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:17.873
(laughing)

00:15:17.873 --> 00:15:20.450
- And he marched into court
with his birth certificate

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:22.140
and sued me,

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:24.470
because he's a whiny little (beeping).

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:26.700
- And in turning the
tables, the very next day,

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:27.760
Trump, through his attorney,

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:29.720
sent Maher a copy of his birth certificate

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:31.387
and demanded that Maher pay him

00:15:31.387 --> 00:15:33.430
$5 million to donate to charity.

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:36.240
And yes, what I'm going to
show you is a real letter

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:38.187
sent and signed by a lawyer.

00:15:38.187 --> 00:15:40.700
"I write on Donald Trump's
behalf to accept your offer

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:43.770
made during the Jay Leno
show on January 7, 2013,

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:45.687
that Mr. Trump prove he is not the quote,

00:15:45.687 --> 00:15:48.790
'spawn of his mother having
sex with an orangutan.'

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:51.852
Attached hereto is a copy of
Mr. Trump's birth certificate

00:15:51.852 --> 00:15:55.180
demonstrating that he is
the son of Fred Trump,

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:56.440
not an orangutan."

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.770
And I want to add that not
only is this a real letter

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:00.920
sent and signed by a lawyer,

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:04.090
this demand was not from
Trump's fixer Michael Cohen.

00:16:04.090 --> 00:16:06.040
This was sent by Cooley LLP,

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:08.680
one of the top international
law firms in the world,

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:11.730
best known for representing
multinational corporations.

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:13.500
The following week, the Cooley attorney

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.577
sent a followup demand
letter stating quote,

00:16:15.577 --> 00:16:17.920
"Mr. Trump has accepted
your offer for $5 million,

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:20.990
provided the necessary
documentation and demanded payment.

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:22.840
You have not honored your obligation."

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:24.470
If you think that those
letters are strange,

00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:25.790
wait until you see the complaint

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.520
they actually filed in court.

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:29.460
Because on February 4th, 2013,

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:32.210
Donald Trump formally sued
Bill Maher in California

00:16:32.210 --> 00:16:35.470
for breach of contract demanding
immediate direct payment

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:38.490
of $5 million to Trump so
that he might donate that

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:40.230
to the charities of his choosing.

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:42.670
The complaint reads like
Donald Trump wrote it himself,

00:16:42.670 --> 00:16:44.170
or at least dictated most of it.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:46.390
And after quoting from Maher's
interview with Jay Leno,

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:48.810
Trump argued that Maher
had made a sincere offer

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:51.260
to pay Trump $5 million
if Trump could prove

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:53.140
that he was not the son of an orangutan.

00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:55.060
And the complaint alleges
that a contract was formed

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:57.590
when Trump performed by
producing his birth certificate

00:16:57.590 --> 00:16:59.830
Maher failed to pay the promised sums,

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:03.000
and thus Maher was in breach
of contract for $5 million.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.600
Though apparently they
thought better of it,

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:05.690
because eight weeks later,

00:17:05.690 --> 00:17:07.490
Donald Trump withdrew the lawsuit.

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:10.330
- We should not be having
frivolous lawsuits like this.

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:12.620
The legal system in this
country is not a joke.

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:15.050
It's not a toy for rich
idiots to play with.

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:17.980
It's not a collection
agency for billionaires.

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:19.680
- And while his fixer, Michael Cohen,

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:21.730
claimed that Trump would soon be filing

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:24.810
an amended complaint, such
a complaint was never filed.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:27.030
Cohen never gave any
reasons for the withdrawal

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:29.370
or why a subsequent
lawsuit was never filed.

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:31.580
Though some legal scholars do point out

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:34.140
that this lawsuit was
complete and utter nonsense,

00:17:34.140 --> 00:17:36.960
and Trump wouldn't actually
be able to recover anything,

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:38.520
also other scholars point out

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:40.580
that California's Anti-SLAPP law,

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:43.050
which punishes those who
file frivolous lawsuits

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:44.480
that seek to chill speech

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:46.100
would have entitled Bill Maher to recover

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:48.050
all of his attorney's fees from Trump

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:50.090
when Maher inevitably prevailed.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:52.380
And if there's one thing that
we know about Donald Trump

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.640
is that he hates paying for attorneys.

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:55.580
Of course, the bottom line is

00:17:55.580 --> 00:17:57.680
that all of these lawyers
who filed these lawsuits

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:00.020
should probably be
disbarred and find new jobs,

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:02.750
because they filed such
frivolous lawsuits.

